WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.117 --> 00:00:02.195
- Okay, I'll take this one.

00:00:02.195 --> 00:00:05.208
Honestly, I'm not a big
fan of Hagrid, so...

00:00:05.208 --> 00:00:07.096
- What? What?

00:00:07.096 --> 00:00:10.596
(upbeat electronic music)

00:00:12.309 --> 00:00:14.034
- Hello, Internet. My name's Sara,

00:00:14.034 --> 00:00:15.855
and welcome to Fan or Failure,

00:00:15.855 --> 00:00:17.350
the show where pop culture fans

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.112
fight to prove their devotion.

00:00:19.112 --> 00:00:21.448
- I am a huge Harry Potter fan.

00:00:21.448 --> 00:00:24.132
It's the book that got me into books.

00:00:24.132 --> 00:00:26.589
- I listen to the audiobooks once a year,

00:00:26.589 --> 00:00:28.327
I used to write fanfiction.

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:29.539
I'm also worried that my friends

00:00:29.539 --> 00:00:30.726
and family care about this a lot,

00:00:30.726 --> 00:00:34.202
and they might disown me if I don't win.

00:00:34.202 --> 00:00:36.120
- If you get a question
right, you get a point.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:36.953
If you get it wrong,

00:00:36.953 --> 00:00:39.987
you have to read an incredibly
disparaging sentence

00:00:39.987 --> 00:00:40.929
about Harry Potter.

00:00:40.929 --> 00:00:41.987
- No.

00:00:41.987 --> 00:00:43.383
- Let's get started.

00:00:43.383 --> 00:00:45.624
- What is the name of the company

00:00:45.624 --> 00:00:48.308
where Vernon Dursley works?

00:00:48.308 --> 00:00:50.549
Is it Bloomturns, Tunnings,

00:00:50.549 --> 00:00:52.549
Furrutons, or Grunnings?

00:00:53.598 --> 00:00:54.612
- Oh no.

00:00:54.612 --> 00:00:55.733
(Kendall laughs)

00:00:55.733 --> 00:00:57.551
(tense music)

00:00:57.551 --> 00:00:59.055
- Oh, my handwriting's quite nice today.

00:00:59.055 --> 00:01:02.256
- All right. Let's see your answers.

00:01:02.256 --> 00:01:03.461
Those are both correct.

00:01:03.461 --> 00:01:07.235
You've avoided humiliation
for the first question.

00:01:07.235 --> 00:01:09.314
How much money do you need

00:01:09.314 --> 00:01:12.525
to include a hot chocolate
with your Knight Bus ticket?

00:01:12.525 --> 00:01:13.358
Is it...

00:01:14.282 --> 00:01:16.032
13 Sickles, 29 Knuts,

00:01:17.173 --> 00:01:19.673
four Sickles, or six Galleons?

00:01:20.806 --> 00:01:22.902
- I have no idea.

00:01:22.902 --> 00:01:23.885
- For hot chocolate?

00:01:23.885 --> 00:01:26.293
- [Sara] For hot chocolate
on the Knight Bus.

00:01:26.293 --> 00:01:28.507
- I don't know how to spell Knuts.

00:01:28.507 --> 00:01:29.407
- Oh shit.

00:01:29.407 --> 00:01:31.169
(laughs)

00:01:31.169 --> 00:01:32.669
- One, two, three.

00:01:34.189 --> 00:01:37.704
Unfortunately, unfortunately,
you're both wrong.

00:01:37.704 --> 00:01:38.537
(laughter)

00:01:38.537 --> 00:01:39.370
- What?

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:41.278
- You're both wrong. It was 13 Sickles.

00:01:41.278 --> 00:01:42.111
- No.

00:01:42.111 --> 00:01:43.092
- That's some expensive hot chocolate.

00:01:43.092 --> 00:01:44.616
- That's super expensive.

00:01:44.616 --> 00:01:45.891
- Oh you're selecting one for me.

00:01:45.891 --> 00:01:46.883
(light xylophone music)

00:01:46.883 --> 00:01:48.883
(sighs)

00:01:49.729 --> 00:01:53.062
- Donald Trump reminds me of Dumbledore.

00:01:56.345 --> 00:02:00.749
- Twilight is a better
story than Harry Potter.

00:02:00.749 --> 00:02:03.570
- Weird you would say that.

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:06.041
Here's your next question folks.

00:02:06.041 --> 00:02:09.507
Wolfsbane and Monkshood are
technically the same plant.

00:02:09.507 --> 00:02:11.696
What is that plant called?

00:02:11.696 --> 00:02:14.363
Is it called Aconite, Tanzanite,

00:02:15.604 --> 00:02:17.521
Melanite, or Baphonite?

00:02:18.912 --> 00:02:19.745
- Hm.

00:02:22.049 --> 00:02:24.098
- Can I tell you what it does instead?

00:02:24.098 --> 00:02:25.562
I can tell you that.
- No, you must choose a name.

00:02:25.562 --> 00:02:27.102
There's no option E.

00:02:27.102 --> 00:02:29.496
- All right. I think...

00:02:29.496 --> 00:02:32.373
- One, two, three, let's see those boards.

00:02:32.373 --> 00:02:34.528
- It looks like Robin is correct.

00:02:34.528 --> 00:02:35.774
- [Kendall] Dammit!

00:02:35.774 --> 00:02:37.293
- It is aconite.

00:02:37.293 --> 00:02:38.126
- No.

00:02:38.126 --> 00:02:40.777
- Kendall, unfortunately
that does me you have to

00:02:40.777 --> 00:02:43.620
read a horrible sentence
about the thing you love.

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.561
- If the Sorting Hat were real,

00:02:45.561 --> 00:02:50.534
it would sort these books into
the trash where they belong.

00:02:50.534 --> 00:02:51.399
- This next game is called...

00:02:51.399 --> 00:02:52.769
Whose eyes are these?

00:02:52.769 --> 00:02:55.656
I'll show you three pictures,
of eyes that I have drawn,

00:02:55.656 --> 00:02:58.434
because I couldn't get the
rights to use the actual photos,

00:02:58.434 --> 00:03:01.094
and you guys will tell
me whose eyes are these?

00:03:01.094 --> 00:03:02.887
And unfortunately, the punishment for this

00:03:02.887 --> 00:03:05.494
is not saying disparaging
sentences about Harry Potter.

00:03:05.494 --> 00:03:08.269
It is, however, ripping
pages from the book.

00:03:08.269 --> 00:03:10.075
- No way.
- No. No.

00:03:10.075 --> 00:03:12.422
- So, pray that you do
not get these wrong.

00:03:12.422 --> 00:03:13.715
- No.

00:03:13.715 --> 00:03:15.201
- Whose eyes are these?

00:03:15.201 --> 00:03:17.268
Whose eyes are these?

00:03:17.268 --> 00:03:18.980
- Are those eyebrows, or is that--

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:20.973
- These are eyebrows, come on.

00:03:20.973 --> 00:03:22.663
You can't tell? I'm offended.

00:03:22.663 --> 00:03:23.578
(laughs)

00:03:23.578 --> 00:03:24.411
- It's from the movie?

00:03:24.411 --> 00:03:27.035
- The books are words.
There's no pictures.

00:03:27.035 --> 00:03:27.868
- You're a pretty good artist.

00:03:27.868 --> 00:03:29.095
- Thank you.

00:03:29.095 --> 00:03:30.845
Whose eyes are these?

00:03:32.036 --> 00:03:34.545
No. These are the eyes of Luna Lovegood.

00:03:34.545 --> 00:03:35.696
- No, they're not.

00:03:35.696 --> 00:03:37.282
- They 100% are.

00:03:37.282 --> 00:03:38.788
And now it is time for your punishment.

00:03:38.788 --> 00:03:39.621
- Oh, god.

00:03:39.621 --> 00:03:41.873
(inhales)

00:03:41.873 --> 00:03:44.635
- Just rip out you thought maybe oh,

00:03:44.635 --> 00:03:46.243
J.K. Rowling's editor should have told her

00:03:46.243 --> 00:03:47.451
to shorten this chapter.

00:03:47.451 --> 00:03:48.600
It's too long, goes on to long.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:49.679
- All right.

00:03:49.679 --> 00:03:52.226
Professor McGonagall's
getting mad at Harry

00:03:52.226 --> 00:03:53.312
and Ron and Hermione.

00:03:53.312 --> 00:03:56.337
- That happens like 20 times.

00:03:56.337 --> 00:03:58.504
(ripping)

00:04:00.793 --> 00:04:01.968
- That's so wrong.

00:04:01.968 --> 00:04:02.801
- I know.

00:04:02.801 --> 00:04:04.647
- Okay, I'll take this one.

00:04:04.647 --> 00:04:06.837
Honestly, I'm not a big
fan of Hagrid, so...

00:04:06.837 --> 00:04:08.754
- Whose eyes are these?

00:04:09.612 --> 00:04:11.204
- Are their pupils meant to be off?

00:04:11.204 --> 00:04:12.624
- Nope. I messed up.

00:04:12.624 --> 00:04:13.457
(laughs)

00:04:13.457 --> 00:04:15.207
- I've got nothing.

00:04:15.207 --> 00:04:17.206
- Let's see em.

00:04:17.206 --> 00:04:18.762
It's unfortunately neither of them.

00:04:18.762 --> 00:04:20.018
- No.

00:04:20.018 --> 00:04:21.029
- It was Remus Lupin's eyes.

00:04:21.029 --> 00:04:21.933
- Dammit, that was my other one.

00:04:21.933 --> 00:04:23.279
- That was going to be my second one, too.

00:04:23.279 --> 00:04:24.312
(groans)

00:04:24.312 --> 00:04:27.042
- Yeah, sometimes second
choice is the better choice.

00:04:27.042 --> 00:04:31.209
- Oh, this is when Hagrid got
drunk and got a dragon egg.

00:04:32.075 --> 00:04:34.239
- I'm gonna rip out child abuse pages,

00:04:34.239 --> 00:04:36.748
from when he's living with the Dursleys.

00:04:36.748 --> 00:04:38.261
- I love those bits.

00:04:38.261 --> 00:04:41.002
(tearing)

00:04:41.002 --> 00:04:44.065
- All right, this is the
last set of eyes I have here.

00:04:44.065 --> 00:04:45.721
Whose eyes are these?

00:04:45.721 --> 00:04:47.558
- And it's like a main character?

00:04:47.558 --> 00:04:50.239
It's not like Madame Hooch or something?

00:04:50.239 --> 00:04:51.500
(laughs)

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:53.917
- No, it's not an obscure strange person.

00:04:53.917 --> 00:04:57.078
- I haven't got the faintest idea.

00:04:57.078 --> 00:04:57.911
(sighs)

00:04:57.911 --> 00:05:01.035
- Let's see those answers
on one, two, three.

00:05:01.035 --> 00:05:02.797
- Unfortunately, those are both wrong.

00:05:02.797 --> 00:05:03.630
- No.

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:05.250
- These were the eyes
of Neville Longbottom.

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:06.083
- No way.

00:05:06.083 --> 00:05:07.249
- They were indeed his eyes.

00:05:07.249 --> 00:05:08.174
He has eyebrows just like--

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:09.373
- Can we see? Can we see?

00:05:09.373 --> 00:05:11.290
- Can you see it again?

00:05:12.727 --> 00:05:14.821
- It is Neville Longbottom.

00:05:14.821 --> 00:05:16.511
- Unfortunately, that
is the end of our game,

00:05:16.511 --> 00:05:20.070
however it does mean
that Robin is the winner,

00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:23.559
that he is the greatest
wizard in all the land.

00:05:23.559 --> 00:05:25.981
And he wins the Golden Critch.

00:05:25.981 --> 00:05:27.476
- It's a Snitch.

00:05:27.476 --> 00:05:29.643
(singing)

00:05:31.467 --> 00:05:33.165
- This is a lemon?

00:05:33.165 --> 00:05:36.748
(upbeat electronic music)

